VeridianOS: _XkbReadKeyActions reports BadAlloc when out of memory

For a reply with 248 or more key actions the per-key action counts are
read into a buffer from Xmallocarray(), whose result was not checked.
_XkbCopyFromReadBuffer() refuses a NULL destination, so nothing was
written through the null pointer, but the failure was reported as
BadLength (a malformed reply) instead of BadAlloc. It now returns
BadAlloc, as the function already does when resizing a key's actions
fails. (Prepared for upstream, gitlab.freedesktop.org/xorg/lib/libx11.)

--- a/src/xkb/XKBGetMap.c
+++ b/src/xkb/XKBGetMap.c
@@ -255,6 +255,8 @@
             numDesc = numDescBuf;
         else
             numDesc = Xmallocarray(nKeyActs, sizeof(CARD8));
+        if (numDesc == NULL)
+            return BadAlloc;
 
         if (!_XkbCopyFromReadBuffer(buf, (char *) numDesc, nKeyActs)) {
             ret = BadLength;
